{"content": "# Race Condition: Explained Simply\n\n## The Core Idea\n\nA **race condition** occurs when the correctness of a program depends on the *timing* or *order* in which threads (or processes) execute. If two or more threads access shared data **simultaneously** and at least one of them modifies it, the final result can be unpredictable \u2014 it \"races\" to see who gets there first.\n\nThink of it like two people trying to edit the same line in a shared document at the exact same time. If they both read the value, then both write their changes, one person's change gets **overwritten** \u2014 and you don't know which one \"won.\"\n\n---\n\n## Concrete Example: A Bank Account\n\nImagine a simple bank account with a balance", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "#", "logprob": -0.8514807546048075, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "#", "logprob": -0.8514807546048075}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -1.7637007558255107}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -1.9849322163967997}, {"token": "Imagine", "logprob": -2.909815105190745}, {"token": "Hey", "logprob": -2.9142649495510966}, {"token": "Think", "logprob": -3.062780650845042}, {"token": "Hi", "logprob": -3.1242373311428935}, {"token": "Hello", "logprob": -3.278948100796214}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -4.182941707363597}, {"token": "What", "logprob": -5.471592220058909}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -6.229635509243479}, {"token": "Welcome", "logprob": -6.672899516811839}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -6.958803447475901}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -6.995447429409495}, {"token": "Thinking", "logprob": -8.16033390401887}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -8.261680873623362}, {"token": "You", "logprob": -8.349954875698558}, {"token": "As", "logprob": -8.366709026089183}, {"token": "Ex", "logprob": -8.705736430874339}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -9.33694294332551}]}, {"token": " Race", "logprob": -0.16831299277551537, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " Race", "logprob": -0.16831299277551537}, {"token": " What", "logprob": -1.94309708091028