{"content": "To find the derivative of the function $f(x) = x^3 \\sin(x)$, we need to use the **Product Rule**.\n\n### 1. Identify the Components\nThe function is a product of two functions:\n*   $u(x) = x^3$\n*   $v(x) = \\sin(x)$\n\n### 2. State the Product Rule\nThe Product Rule states that for a function $f(x) = u(x)v(x)$, the derivative is:\n$$ \\frac{d}{dx}[u(x)v(x)] = u'(x)v(x) + u(x)v'(x) $$\n\n### 3. Differentiate Each Component\nFirst, we find the derivatives of $u(x)$ and $v(x)$ separately", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "To", "logprob": -0.010532887434127503, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "To", "logprob": -0.010532887434127503}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -5.631790669416549}, {"token": "This", "logprob": -7.040746243452194}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -7.127652676557663}, {"token": "We", "logprob": -7.18270448014653}, {"token": " To", "logprob": -7.237787754987838}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -7.610789807294967}, {"token": "Let", "logprob": -8.077095540022018}, {"token": "Since", "logprob": -8.267183812116745}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -8.568266423200729}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -8.70059827134526}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -8.835677655195358}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -8.942123921369674}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -9.181513340925338}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -9.22326901719487}, {"token": "For", "logprob": -9.35301640794194}, {"token": "When", "logprob": -9.367811711286667}, {"token": "Finding", "logprob": -9.765018017744186}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -9.870964558576706}, {"token": "You", "logprob": -9.915691884016159}]}, {"token": " find", "logprob": -0.003034030539971866, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " find", "logprob": -0.003034030539971866}, {"token": " differentiate", "logprob": -6.328895007712823}, {"token": " calculate", "logprob": -7.382085239036066}, {"token": " solve", "logprob": -9.113933002097589}, {"token": " determine", "logprob": -9.239794170005304}, {"token": " finding", "logprob": -10.075157558066827}, {"tok