{"content": "```bash\nfind . -name \"*.py\" -exec cat {} + | wc -l\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- `find . -name \"*.py\"` \u2014 finds all `.py` files under the current directory (recursively).\n- `-exec cat {} +` \u2014 concatenates the contents of all found files (the `+` form is more efficient than `\\;` as it batches arguments).\n- `| wc -l` \u2014 counts the total number of lines.\n\n**Alternative (if you want to handle filenames with spaces more robustly):**\n\n```bash\nfind . -name \"*.py\" -print0 | xargs -0 cat | wc -l\n```\n\nThis uses null-delimited output (`-print0`) and `xargs -", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "```", "logprob": -0.046665179131025525, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "```", "logprob": -0.046665179131025525}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -3.4241752499318068}, {"token": "`", "logprob": -5.7498512142872755}, {"token": "find", "logprob": -6.135646807548994}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -6.304790484306807}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -6.32406614959001}, {"token": "You", "logprob": -7.355033861992354}, {"token": "This", "logprob": -7.799072253105635}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -7.909988390800947}, {"token": "Find", "logprob": -8.19125364959001}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -8.648967730400557}, {"token": "Use", "logprob": -8.7343788021779}, {"token": "bash", "logprob": -8.949003207085127}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -9.041137682793135}, {"token": "#!/", "logprob": -9.050077425835127}, {"token": "<tool_call>", "logprob": -9.168004977104658}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -9.19314573943376}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -9.272994982597822}, {"token": "One", "logprob": -9.333740221855635}, {"token": "B", "logprob": -9.512107836601729}]}, {"token": "bash", "logprob": -0.0004037136566097388, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "bash", "logprob": -0.0004037136566097388}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -8.457345318270868}, {"token": " bash", "logprob": -9.492898296786493}, {"token": "sh", "logprob": -9.521985363436883}, {"token": "awk", "logprob": -12.4263804668914