{"content": "Here are the eight planets of our solar system, listed in order from the Sun, along with one interesting fact about each:\n\n1. **Mercury**  \n   *Fact:* Despite being the closest planet to the Sun, it is not the hottest. Venus is hotter due to its thick, greenhouse-effect atmosphere. Mercury\u2019s surface temperature can swing from -173\u00b0C (-280\u00b0F) at night to 427\u00b0C (800\u00b0F) during the day.\n\n2. **Venus**  \n   *Fact:* Venus rotates in the opposite direction to most planets (retrograde rotation). This means the Sun rises in the west and sets in the east. A day on Venus (one full rotation) is longer than its year (one orbit around the", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.0018680255662850698, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.0018680255662850698}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -7.123619810844605}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -8.767992750908082}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -9.163538710380738}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -9.342678801323121}, {"token": "Our", "logprob": -9.38835217168445}, {"token": "Note", "logprob": -9.726033942009156}, {"token": "Mer", "logprob": -10.161843077446168}, {"token": "While", "logprob": -10.473349348808473}, {"token": "Sure", "logprob": -10.638417021537965}, {"token": "As", "logprob": -10.64371754338855}, {"token": "Since", "logprob": -10.64879967382068}, {"token": " Here", "logprob": -10.686522261406129}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -10.801586882377809}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -11.057286040092652}, {"token": "Of", "logprob": -11.150414244438355}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -11.285239950920289}, {"token": "here", "logprob": -11.380431906486695}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -11.444679991508668}, {"token": "Interesting", "logprob": -11.49446560552234}]}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -0.1285761726903374, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " are", "logprob": -0.1285761726903374}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -2.117460144858306}, {"token": "\u2019s", "logprob": -8.591977967