{"content": "A hash map is a data structure that stores key-value pairs. It uses a **hash function** to compute an index (or \"bucket\") in an underlying array where the value is stored.\n\nA **collision** occurs when two different keys produce the same hash index. Since the array slot can only hold one item directly, the hash map must have a strategy to handle this situation.\n\nHere are the two primary methods used to handle collisions:\n\n### 1. Chaining (Separate Chaining)\nIn this method, each slot in the hash table's array contains a pointer to a linked list (or another data structure like a tree).\n\n*   **Mechanism**:\n    1.  When a key is inserted, the hash function calculates the index.\n   ", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "A", "logprob": -0.3698096699232032, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "A", "logprob": -0.3698096699232032}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -1.4485087818616798}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -3.740233940553086}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -3.763743919801133}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -4.45552782483043}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -5.454013390015977}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -5.8000026173108985}, {"token": "Hash", "logprob": -6.238189262818711}, {"token": "When", "logprob": -6.8318934864515235}, {"token": "Coll", "logprob": -7.083499474000352}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -7.4471583790296485}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -7.56636766858043}, {"token": "Since", "logprob": -7.694324058961289}, {"token": "Handling", "logprob": -8.053073448609727}, {"token": "At", "logprob": -8.295396370362656}, {"token": "Collision", "logprob": -8.366561455201524}, {"token": "How", "logprob": -8.487987083863633}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -9.062101883363145}, {"token": "Understanding", "logprob": -9.390137237977402}, {"token": "Data", "logprob": -9.584628624390977}]}, {"token": " hash", "logprob": -0.41846502912130745, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " hash", "logprob": -0.41846502912130745}, {"token": " **", "logprob": -1.3125861991652528}, {"token": " 