{"content": "```c\n#include <stddef.h>\n\n/**\n * Reverses a null-terminated string in place.\n *\n * @param str Pointer to the null-terminated string to reverse.\n */\nvoid reverse_string(char *str) {\n    if (str == NULL) {\n        return;\n    }\n\n    char *left = str;\n    char *right = str;\n\n    // Find the end of the string (pointing to the null terminator)\n    while (*right != '\\0') {\n        right++;\n    }\n\n    // Move right back to the last non-null character\n    if (right != str) {\n        right--;\n    }\n\n    // Swap characters from both ends moving inward\n    while (left", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "```", "logprob": -0.017322661114310023, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "```", "logprob": -0.017322661114310023}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -4.401563765240287}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -5.774726988506888}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -7.277019621563529}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -8.28486645383892}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -8.491607786846732}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -9.062015654278373}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -9.317350508404349}, {"token": "I", "logprob": -9.461620451641654}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -10.096929671002005}, {"token": "C", "logprob": -10.449529768658255}, {"token": "Re", "logprob": -10.490167738628958}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -10.631140829754447}, {"token": "This", "logprob": -10.707607390118216}, {"token": "#include", "logprob": -10.879235388470267}, {"token": "function", "logprob": -10.962206961346244}, {"token": "Below", "logprob": -11.339100958538626}, {"token": "c", "logprob": -11.525117994976615}, {"token": "//", "logprob": -11.545566679668998}, {"token": "You", "logprob": -11.57176888151226}]}, {"token": "c", "logprob": -2.5258908831204963e-05, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "c", "logprob": -2.5258908831204963e-05}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -11.404757009397112}, {"token": "cpp", "logprob": -11.601404653440081}, {"token": " c", "logprob": -13.693537221799456}, {"token": "typescript", "logprob"