{"content": "In simple terms, **compound interest** is when you earn interest not just on your original money, but also on the interest you\u2019ve already earned.\n\nThink of it as **\"interest on interest.\"**\n\n### A Simple Analogy:\nImagine you have a snowball rolling down a hill.\n- **Simple Interest**: The snowball stays the same size, but you keep adding a small amount of snow to it every day. It grows slowly and steadily.\n- **Compound Interest**: The snowball gets bigger as it rolls. Because it\u2019s bigger, it picks up *more* snow with each turn. The bigger it gets, the faster it grows. This is exponential growth.\n\n### A Real-Life Example:\nLet\u2019s say you invest **$1,000", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "In", "logprob": -0.6774416105569045, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "In", "logprob": -0.6774416105569045}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -0.8181829588235061}, {"token": "Compound", "logprob": -3.6125288145363967}, {"token": "Think", "logprob": -4.5846586363137405}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -4.6781911985696}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -6.739741338950459}, {"token": "Simple", "logprob": -7.359915746909444}, {"token": "Simply", "logprob": -7.480765356284444}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -7.981917394858662}, {"token": "Imagine", "logprob": -8.193594946128194}, {"token": "Here", "logprob": -8.367606176596944}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -8.426999105674092}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -9.027649893027608}, {"token": "Comp", "logprob": -9.094491018515889}, {"token": "At", "logprob": -9.70310403273708}, {"token": "You", "logprob": -9.810503019553487}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -10.047778143149678}, {"token": "If", "logprob": -10.526072515708272}, {"token": "Thinking", "logprob": -10.57707692549831}, {"token": "Let", "logprob": -10.78544045851833}]}, {"token": " simple", "logprob": -0.0027403202859055398, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " simple", "logprob": -0.0027403202859055398}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -6.140132364353288}, {"token": " simplest", 