{"content": "The capital of Australia is **Canberra**.\n\n### Why isn't it Sydney?\n\nThe choice of Canberra as the capital was primarily the result of a **political compromise** between the two largest and most powerful cities in Australia: **Sydney** (in New South Wales) and **Melbourne** (in Victoria).\n\nHere\u2019s a breakdown of the key reasons:\n\n1. **Political Rivalry**:  \n   In the late 19th century, as the Australian colonies moved toward federation (becoming a single nation), Sydney and Melbourne were both vying to be the capital. Neither city\u2019s state government was willing to concede to the other. Sydney, as the largest city and economic hub, felt it should be the capital. Melbourne, which had been the de facto capital", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.0029252915997552975, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "The", "logprob": -0.0029252915997552975}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -5.940076246799951}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -8.531991377415185}, {"token": " The", "logprob": -10.785281553806787}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -11.224131956638818}, {"token": "Capital", "logprob": -11.790345564426904}, {"token": "Actually", "logprob": -12.481092825474267}, {"token": "Yes", "logprob": -12.754565611423974}, {"token": "It", "logprob": -12.829903975071435}, {"token": "While", "logprob": -12.90206469589663}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -12.960114851536279}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -12.979760542454247}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -13.09208048874331}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -13.124575987400537}, {"token": "There", "logprob": -13.712478056492333}, {"token": "No", "logprob": -13.752841368259912}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -13.826570883335595}, {"token": "Although", "logprob": -13.893968000950341}, {"token": "As", "logprob": -13.904021635593896}, {"token": "<think>", "logprob": -13.914992704929833}]}, {"token": " capital", "logprob": -9.536542900789868e-05, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " capital", "logprob": -9.536542900789868e-05}, {"